  "limitations": [
    "Eager JIT and synchronous GC remain defaults; concurrent/shared-worker and lazy-JIT experiments do not establish general performance claims.",
    "macOS measurements use a loaded development host; cross-host measurements are not controlled speedup comparisons.",
    "Windows native file output remains unsupported. PostgreSQL is included and qualified on macOS only.",
    "Expanded native JSON mapper consumers currently require HTTP host bindings; minimal-host retention remains a gap.",
    "Native signal execution remains blocked by unit boxing; Neo.Signals is excluded from the standard library bundle.",
    "HTTP callback faults allow only the two documented native entry callers after shared inner frames; causal async stack stitching remains limited.",
    "Separate SDK and VSIX dependency attribution is supplied in the matching companion raven-tool-notices archives."
  ]
